    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Npcap/Wireshark presence enumeration", "technique": "T1040", "what_happened": "At 2032-08-26 11:08:08 UTC on WS-OPS-14, AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock issuing Test-Path on HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\npcap AND HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Wireshark, reading ImagePath and Start type. Rule 92201 triggered (low-fidelity informational).", "chain_reason": "Reading the npcap service registry key and Wireshark install location is the precondition step of a packet-capture attack: the attacker checks whether the packet-driver toolchain is already installed and what its driver path is."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "pktmon component list + filter add for credential-bearing ports", "technique": "T1040", "what_happened": "At 2032-08-26 11:08:18, Sysmon EID 1 captured 'pktmon.exe component list' then 5 successive 'pktmon.exe filter add -p <port>' commands for ports 80 (HTTP), 53 (DNS), 88 (Kerberos), 445 (SMB), 389 (LDAP), with parent powershell.exe. Rule 92200 triggered.", "chain_reason": "pktmon filter add for ports 80+53+88+445+389 is a deliberately credential-focused filter set: HTTP basic auth, DNS for hostname/identity leakage, Kerberos AS-REQ/TGS-REQ, SMB / NTLM authentication, LDAP plaintext bind. No legitimate diagnostic workflow targets exactly these 5 ports."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "pktmon start capture to .etl + 5s collection window", "technique": "T1040", "what_happened": "At 2032-08-26 11:08:38, Sysmon EID 1 captured 'pktmon.exe start --etw -p 0 -f C:\\Users\\l.ferraro\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p142_pcap_110808\\cap.etl' with parent powershell.exe. Sysmon EID 11 confirmed creation of cap.etl (8.4 MB after 5s capture). 5 seconds later: 'pktmon.exe stop' captured.", "chain_reason": "pktmon active capture writes raw frames to an ETL file. With the credential-port filter set (Q2), every TGT/TGS, NTLM challenge-response, and HTTP Basic header transiting the wire during the capture window is in the file."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "pktmon format → text output + AMSI tool literals", "technique": "T1040", "what_happened": "At 2032-08-26 11:08:50, Sysmon EID 1 captured 'pktmon.exe format C:\\Users\\l.ferraro\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p142_pcap_110808\\cap.etl -o C:\\Users\\l.ferraro\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p142_pcap_110808\\cap.txt' producing a human-readable text dump of the captured frames. AMSI EID 4104 captured scriptblock literals: 'netsh trace start capture=yes provider=\"Microsoft-Windows-TCPIP\" tracefile=cap.etl', 'tshark.exe -i 1 -w cap.pcap -a duration:60', 'WinDump.exe -i 1 -w cap.pcap', 'New-NetEventPacketCaptureProvider'. Rule 92202 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Converting ETL to text + AMSI references to tshark / WinDump / netsh trace = full packet-capture toolkit awareness. The text output gives the attacker offline-analyzable plaintext / captured-hash content."}
